        <remarks>
          <para>Sets the dim brightness of the display.</para>
          <para>The system will use this brightness value whenever the display should be dim, i.e. it is powered on and dimmed due to user activity or app activity.</para>
          <para>Value of 0.0 indicates the minimum supported brightness and value of 1.0 indicates the maximum supported brightness.</para>
          <para>If set, the default brightness must also be set to a value greater or equal to the dim brightness. If unset, defaults to the system default.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/hardware/display/VirtualDisplayConfig.Builder#setDimBrightness(float)" title="Reference documentation">Android reference for <code>android.hardware.display.VirtualDisplayConfig.Builder.setDimBrightness</code>.</a></format></para>
